    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d747">

                <pb facs="0809" n="797" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg797"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/13484b: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the
                        Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-07-27T16:00:00-04:00">July 27, 1941—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>930. The President has instructed Harry Hopkins,<anchor n="42" xml:id="d747-f1"/>
                    who is now in London, to proceed by air to Moscow. He will be leaving Monday
                        night<anchor n="43" xml:id="d747-f2"/> via Archangel. The objective of his
                    mission is primarily to <pb facs="0810" n="798" xml:id="pg798"/> investigate how
                    best we can furnish material assistance to the Soviet Union at this time. The
                    details of his mission he will himself explain to you upon his arrival.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
